retrace (2.13.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Added: live Windows hooks end to end -- inline hook ->
    assembly wrapper -> engine -> trampoline; fopen (ucrt,
    default) plus the opt-in ntdll set (NtCreateFile, NtOpenFile,
    NtQueryAttributesFile, NtClose, LdrLoadDll) with
    OBJECT_ATTRIBUTES/UNICODE_STRING path decoders.
  * Added: PE-section registry (.rtrA/.rtrF/.rtrD walked via the
    module's own PE headers) replacing the empty-registry staging
    -- actions/prototypes/datatypes register on Windows (MSVC and
    MinGW, no constructors needed).
  * Added: retrace-win-run launcher and a single injectable
    retrace.dll (engine + hook core + backend; previously the
    backend DLL shipped without the engine).
  * Security: ntdll hooks are strictly opt-in
    (RETRACE_WIN_NTDLL=1); AV/EDR sensitivity documented in
    docs/windows.md.

 -- Ribose Inc <opensource@ribose.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0000

retrace (2.12.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Added: retrace-profile -- claims-vs-truth risk profiler
    (functions, file accesses, env, net) with kernel-layer delta
    (sub-libc detection), static capability scan, and --jail-out
    deny-by-default sandbox policy emission.
  * Added: retrace-strace2retrace (Linux kernel-truth converter).
  * Added: sandbox action allow_paths mode (deny-by-default);
    path params found via prototype metadata; failures fail
    closed with EACCES.
  * Added: offline analysis tools (correlate, procmon2retrace,
    strace2retrace, profile) now build on Windows.
  * Changed: log_params entries carry the function name so
    offline tools can attribute calls without banner parsing.

 -- Ribose Inc <opensource@ribose.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

retrace (2.11.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: fopen interception silently bypassed on macOS for
    every target compiled with _DARWIN_C_SOURCE (the project's
    own CMake adds it to all Darwin targets): modern SDKs emit
    fopen$DARWIN_EXTSN in optimized builds. The variant symbol
    is now interposed; the engine strips the suffix so configs,
    prototypes, and logs use the plain name.

